Array:- List of Elements of the same type placed in a contiguous memory location.
  Note:- Arrays are static type means if define an array of a particular size you can't add more than that.
Note:- Arrays are Pass by Reference means if you pass an array as function argument and made changes to it, it will also reflects changes 
        in the main function too ( or the original array).
Operations in Arrays:- Create, Input, Ouput, Update
Indexing starts from 0
Creating an Array:-   
                      dataType arrayName[] = new dataType[size];  // declaring an Array
                      eg, int marks[] = new int[3];
                      int marks[] = {50,60,90};          // declaring and initializing an array of size 3
                          marks[0]=50;
                          marks[1]=60;
                          marks[2]=90;
                      // Taking input in an array after declaring
                      for(int i=0;i<marks.length;i++){            // Note:- Length of the array=  Using length property eg, arrayName.length;
                          marks[i]=sc.next();
                      }
